esign"],"pub":["Amanita Design"],"released":"May 7, 2012","meta":82,"langs":["English","German","French","Italian","Spanish - Spain","Russian","Japanese","Polish","Czech","Simplified Chinese"],"min":[["OS","Microsoft\u00ae Windows\u00ae XP/Vista/7/8/10"],["Processor","1.6 Ghz Processor"],["Memory","1 GB RAM"],["DirectX\u00ae","5.0"],["Hard Drive","550 MB HD space"]],"rec":[],"deck":3,"blurb":"Botanicula is a humor-filled point-and-click adventure from Amanita Design, the studio behind Machinarium and Samorost. Five little tree creatures set out to save the last seed of their home tree from evil parasites that are draining it of life.\n\nThere is no dialogue. Instead you poke, click and experiment with everything on screen, and almost everything reacts with a funny animation or sound. The puzzles are gentle, and the music by Czech band DVA is a big part of its charm. It is a lovely, relaxed game for all ages."}}